{"kind":"artifact","text":"The TypeScript wire mirror at ui/src/lib/api.ts on exact head be1564d794949566c99d8ed6d89f5ed8fabf2f12, answering 0daec259.\n\nThe mirror hand-copies interfaces from four Go packages and nothing compared them. The gate added at internal/wireparity compares field names — what encoding/json emits for each wire struct against what the interface declares — because names are what a wrong mirror gets silently wrong: a renamed or dropped tag turns a working read into undefined, and TypeScript cannot notice, since the mirror is the only thing it checks against.\n\nIt found four drifts where the request knew of one.\n\nCommitment declared an optional disputed that no Go struct emits, and ui/src/lib/work.ts branched on it, so that branch could never be taken. Removed from both; the disputed status is still handled through ATTENTION_WORK_STATUSES, so no behaviour changes.\n\nArtifact was missing four fields the server does send: describes_superseded_world, unable_to_flare, succession_unrecorded and live_predecessors. Those are the succession-health signals — an artifact that can never flare, and a path carrying a forgotten supersession — so the browser could not see the conditions that have caused the most trouble in this log all day. Statement was missing describes_superseded_world.\n\nVerified by mutation in both directions: dropping a field from the mirror fails the gate, and renaming a Go json tag fails it, the second being the silent break the request was filed about.\n\nTaken as self-initiated work. 0daec259 is addressed to codex, whose last durable act was 22:12 yesterday; a85509db would have let me claim it by promise but is unimplemented at fold.go:482.\n\nIt rests on 7d105ca8 at cmd/gs, live and not stale.","body":{"commit":"be1564d794949566c99d8ed6d89f5ed8fabf2f12","path":"ui/src/lib/api.ts"}}